{"title": "The Motorola Signature 27’s haptics finally feel more like a Pixel, and it’s about time", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/26/the-motorola-signature-27s-haptics-finally-feel-more-like-a-pixel-and-its-about-time/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/motorola-signature-27-back-texture-olive-02-1.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Motorola has been content with mid-grade haptics for years, but the Motorola Signature 27’s haptics rightfully upgrade the experience.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/26/the-motorola-signature-27s-haptics-finally-feel-more-like-a-pixel-and-its-about-time/#more-740155\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-26T06:36:19+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-26T19:30:24.639998+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Big Google Home update adds these new Nest Cam, app, and Gemini features", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/google-home-update-nest-cam-thermostat-gemini-features/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/07/google-home-speaker-nest-hub-1.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Google Home is rolling out <em>another</em> big update, this time adding features and bringing improvements across Nest Cam, Nest Thermostarts, Gemini, and more.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/google-home-update-nest-cam-thermostat-gemini-features/#more-740407\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-25T12:50:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-26T19:30:24.639998+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "9to5Google’s Best of 2026", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/9to5googles-best-of-2026/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/9to5google-best-of-2026-feature-composite.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/feature/review/\">reviewed dozens of products in 2026</a>, and the one through line across all of them was cost. Because of RAMageddon, everything was more expensive, and it became somewhat easier to separate the products that were good because they were cheap from the ones that were good at any price.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This year was a lot of things, but it was primarily a reminder that the best products are created through careful iteration. Only one product on this list, the XREAL Aura, represents an emerging class. The rest, from the Fitbit Air to the Samsung Galaxy Z Fold 8, showcase years of work in optimizing for design, weight, battery life, and performance. Some take more risks than others, but to us they all represent the very best of their respective categories.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/9to5googles-best-of-2026/#more-740020\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-25T11:29:37+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-26T19:30:24.639998+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "‘Enough Phone’ is stuffing a bigger battery, more RAM & storage into its small Android phone at no extra cost", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/enough-phone-ram-storage-battery-upgrades/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/enough-phone-1.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The “Enough Phone” is trying to fulfill the small Android phone dream and, now, it’s getting some spec upgrades to the battery, RAM, and storage, all with no added cost.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/enough-phone-ram-storage-battery-upgrades/#more-740360\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-25T10:10:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-26T19:30:24.639998+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Hello Weather is the best Apple Weather app on Android", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/hello-weather-android-apple/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/Hello-Weather-cover.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While Pixel Weather serves my needs quite well, I’ve been looking for a way to check Apple Weather (previously Dark Sky) forecast data on Android, and I’ve finally found it with <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.helloweatherapp\">Hello Weather by Electric Dream Machine</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/hello-weather-android-apple/#more-740363\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-25T09:44:03+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-26T19:30:24.639998+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Save serious money with RedPocket Mobile’s $5 Black Friday plans", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/save-serious-money-with-redpockets-black-friday-plans-that-start-at-5-a-month-sponsored/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/00947cc8ee4c3fe022e46888fd9a63f8_abt-us-mob.webp?w=1536\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You’re not going to believe this, but there’s one part of your life that’s not actually getting more expensive. If you <a href=\"https://www.redpocket.com/shop?utm_source=9to5&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=9to5_article\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow\">switch to RedPocket Mobile</a> during its Black Friday sale, you can ditch your costly carrier and get a plan that starts at $5 per month. It’s not too good to be true: RedPocket has been around for 20 years, and unlike most MVNOs, it’s independently owned and operated. That gives it the ability to offer you real network choice when you sign up for a new plan (we’ll explain more later), and keeps your costs low. Really low.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/save-serious-money-with-redpockets-black-friday-plans-that-start-at-5-a-month-sponsored/#more-735678\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-25T08:41:47+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-26T19:30:24.639998+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
