{"title": "Google Messages replacing old Gemini with new ‘tasks’ chat, and it’s very proactive", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/24/google-messages-gemini-tasks/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/03/gemini-logo.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Last week, Google announced that Gemini tasks (previously called Spark) is now <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/17/gemini-tasks-free/\">available to free users</a> in the US, along with an <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/17/email-text-with-gemini/\">integration in Google Messages</a>. In testing, I’ve found this instance of Gemini to be proactive and feel more like an assistant than the Gemini app does.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/24/google-messages-gemini-tasks/#more-740098\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-24T13:11:31+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-26T19:30:24.639998+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
